    <h2 id="your-vault">3. Your vault is your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Stillroom has no server and no account, and we never have a copy of your files, your password, your recovery key
      or your emergency kit. That’s the point of it, and it means:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>If you forget your password and lose your recovery key and enough kit pieces, nobody can open your vault,
        not even us.</strong> We can’t reset it, recover it or get your files back.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keeping backups is up to you. The app makes encrypted backups and can export everything as ordinary files; please
        use them.
      </li>
      <li>
        The app has limits, documented plainly in our <a href="/security/">security rules</a>: for example, it doesn’t
        protect against a weak password or against malware with administrator rights while the vault is open, and the
        decoy is protection against thieves and abusers, not police.
      </li>
    </ul>

